   "x": 4,
   "y": 5,
   "text": [
    "Joseph Williamson was a tobacco merchant who made a fortune and spent it on tunnels. Under Edge Hill there are miles of brick arches, vaults and passages, and nobody knows why he dug them.",
    "One theory is that it was work for returning soldiers after the Napoleonic wars. Another is that he enjoyed it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "x": 18,
   "y": 6,
   "text": [
    "A chamber of bricked-up arches. The tunnels were largely filled with rubbish and rubble after Williamson died in 1840, and volunteers have been digging them out again for years.",
    "In a gap in the rubble, a few coins. Someone's lucky day."
   ],
